WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.160
Raise the anchor!

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.570
Release the sails!
Depart!

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Mother, I'm leaving!</i>

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.310
<i>Our ship, the Hispaniola, is finally leaving Bristol!</i>

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.360
<i>Mother, I'm leaving!</i>

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.830
<i>My dear, can you hear the bell
that announces their departure?</i>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.670
<i>It's in Bristol, so you can't hear it from here.</i>

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.830
<i>What? Why didn't I go to watch the departure?</i>

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.590
<i>You think I want him to leave? Don't you worry, dear.</i>

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.640
<i>A mother doesn't need to watch her son leave.</i>

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.400
<i>Because she knows...</i>

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.330
<i>...that no matter where her son is,</i>

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:19.100
<i>she will always have a place in her heart for him.</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.970
Treasure
Island

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.770
Takarajima

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.580
saa ikou

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.580
Come, let's go

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.510
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.510
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.390
umi hedeyou

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.390
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.310
ikute ni wa

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.310
Many of us

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.310
minna mada shiranai

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.310
Still don't know of

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.060
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.060
The days and nights full of mystery

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.560
matte iru darou

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.560
That await us there

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.070
itsumo shinji you

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.070
We must always have trust

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.320
magokoro wo

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.320
And be sincere

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.580
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.580
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.710
tade hitotsu no

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.710
I only...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.130
akogare dake wa

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.130
...have one desire

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.420
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.420
And no one...

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:35.130
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:35.130
...will ever take it away

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.680
tade hitotsu no

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.680
I only...

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.980
akogare dake wa

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.980
...have one desire

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.310
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.310
And no one...

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:54.240
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:54.240
...will ever take it away

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.050
episode

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.050
Ol' Barbecue
\h     is a Tough Guy

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.320
So Jim, how does it feel?

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.330
Yes!
It's fantastic!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.720
My shadow is being reflected on the water! Look!

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.420
The sea's somewhat mystical.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.330
At every departure, my heart
beats like it did the first time.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.890
Surely it's the same for Captain Flint.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.770
Captain Flint?

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.230
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.040
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.800
Hey, Captain Flint, I know how you feel.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.490
There's no need to be so rowdy!

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.080
So, the parrot is named Captain Flint?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.040
Yes, I gave him that name in
memory of the famous pirate.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.840
Oh, so that's what it was.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.200
For a moment I thought there were pirates on board.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:01.300
Hey, you still think that I'm a pirate?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.960
No, not at all.
I don't think that anymore.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.310
You rascal.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:13.390
Captain Flint is about two-hundred years old.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.280
Really, two-hundred years old?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.640
Yeah, he was already old the day I met him.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.360
This parrot has traveled the sea
much more than I have.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.160
He seems to have a great time.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.000
I suspect he belonged to pirates.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.170
With them he must have learned to say "pieces of eight".

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.960
The phrase "pieces of eight"...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.020
...refers to an ancient treasure that some pirates have searched for in vain all their life.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:49.220
It is said that there lies a ship full of 350.000 pieces of eight sunken in the Caribbean sea.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:54.520
He was definitely with pirates who wanted to get their hands on that treasure.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.220
How I envy him.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.820
Let's go.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.610
It's time for me to make the meal for the crew.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.080
So, see you later.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.660
Okay, got it!

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.700
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.000
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.330
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.710
Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.130
Pieces of eigh—

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.840
What are you doing?!
That's dangerous!

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.590
You really are a kid.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.510
What?!
Dare say that again, Puppy!

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:34.360
I mean, a young'un like you doesn't know anything about life.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.600
Young'un?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.670
Yeah, you heard me.
And why are you being nice to him?

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.560
He's just the cook.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.530
The only advantage you'll have is extra food.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.640
You should be nice to the captain.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.440
'Cause after all, he's the only master on board.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.720
Anyway, you should seriously consider it.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:11.550
Enemy ship on the horizon!
Just kidding!

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.310
What are you doing here?

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.020
I'm studying!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.320
Ah, I just discovered Captain Smollett!
Just kiddin'.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.110
A cabin boy has nothing to do here!

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:32.370
Go on boy, get out of here.
Hurry up!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.830
I'm not called "boy".
My name is Jim Hawkins!

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:39.420
Cabin boy Jim Hawkins, leave here at once!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.500
Aye-aye!

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:54.220
<i>Log book, first day at sea.</i>

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.410
<i>We have just left Bristol.</i>

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.780
<i>The weather is beautiful, but the sea is rough.</i>

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:03.820
<i>Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey have already suffered seasickness.</i>

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.530
<i>Especially Mr. Trelawney has it bad.</i>

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.410
Master, are you alright?

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.100
Is Treasure Island still far off?

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:20.180
Livesey, why do ships have to travel on the sea?

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.170
Please, Trelawney, don't make me talk.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.370
There, it's ready.
You can bring it to them.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:39.980
Aye.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.190
Listen, Jim.
That soup is special.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.080
I've added herbs that fight seasickness.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.400
Tell that to our two friends.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.820
Aye-aye, sir!

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:01.220
It's strange. I feel like I'm
regaining all my strength.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:04.710
My word, it's true.
My headache is gone.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.420
Of course, it's a special soup.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.640
I feel much better.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.340
I was right, he's an excellent master cook.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.810
Kindly thank him for us, Jim.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.270
Aye-aye, sir!

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.690
Really? Their seasickness has completely disappeared?

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.320
Sure did.
Your soup worked.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.560
Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey were very pleased.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:38.940
I see, that's good to hear.
My soup worked? That's a first.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:43.910
To be honest, there's nothing special about it. It's an ordinary soup.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.860
See Jim, if you tell people that it'll cure them,
their sickness will disappear like magic, right?

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.940
Silver, you old devil!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.140
All hands on deck!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.730
Orders from the captain! We must swab the deck!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.020
Go!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.020
To the deck!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.790
Excuse me, First Mate.
I didn't see you there.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.960
Oh -hic- no...
Excuse me, kid.

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:38.950
Seriously?
The first mate is seasick too?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.510
Seasickness, my boot.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:45.100
It's actually booze.
He's completely drunk.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.350
What? No way! I thought that
alcohol was banned on the ship.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.360
But the fact remains, he was indeed drunk.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:56.780
I would like to know where he found that alcohol.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.830
If the captain ever found out,
there'd be trouble for him.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:22.300
Hey, Barbecue!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.100
Don't you have an entertaining song?

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.770
He's right, Barbecue!
Sing us an old song!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.990
Very well, mates.
I'll sing you one.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.320
Whoa, incredible!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.990
One, two!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:49.980
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.580
Yo-ho-ho and a bottle of rum!

00:10:54.580 --> 00:11:00.920
Drink and the devil had done for the rest!

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.790
<i>That was the song that Billy Bones
sung all the time.</i>

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:07.460
<i>However, when he sang...</i>

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:09.890
<i>...I found it very sad.</i>

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.600
<i>But now that I hear these sailors singing on board,</i>

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:18.320
<i>it's very strange...
I find it oddly joyful!</i>

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:38.300
Captain, it's high time
you take a look at this.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.940
This is a copy of the original map.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:45.430
We have removed the directions to where the treasure is.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.440
Anyway, we must find
the location of this island.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:53.060
How about it, Captain?
Think you can take us there?

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:57.350
Like I have said already,
we are on the right route.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:59.360
For that was the job assigned to me.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:00.990
So tell me.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.120
Now that you've seen the map,
how many days do you think it will it take?

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.940
You can take back your map.

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:13.100
It won't be of any use until
we're close to the island.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.780
I will ask again when I have need of it.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.820
You want something else?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.810
Why the devil are you so formal?!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.510
I came with this map for a good reason.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:30.850
We have to decide who should
bring the treasure back to you.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.900
That is why I'm here!

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.100
That doesn't interest me.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:38.980
The captain's pay that we agreed on will suffice.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.150
Calm yourself, Mr. Trelawney.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:47.480
Geez, what insolence!
Who does he think he is?!

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.980
That captain does not please me!

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.460
Calm down. It's his character.
He's not a bad guy.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.020
To me, he's a perfect captain.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:57.840
Really, you think so?

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:15.020
What's this?

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.780
Captain!
Captain Smollett!

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:21.340
Why did you tie up the sails?

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:22.900
We can't move now.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.820
Without wind, there's no point in releasing the sails.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:30.340
The wind ceased overnight. It's a "dead calm".

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:33.090
We'll have to wait until it picks up again.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.650
In a fog like this, we risk losing our way.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:41.710
We've anchored to prevent the ship from drifting.

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.130
Just act as if it were Sunday.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.100
Take this opportunity to rest in your cabins.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:53.780
There isn't much we can do.
Let's go, Dr. Livesey.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.520
We don't really have a choice.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:59.510
It'll be pretty boring, this "Sunday".

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:02.980
Jim, you go back to your cabin and read a good book.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:05.940
Spend the day off in my cabin?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.490
On a day like this,

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.410
it's best not to hang around on deck.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.520
Why's that?

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:13.900
Don't worry.
I suggest you listen to me.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.790
Well now, I'll return to my cabin too and take a nap.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:17.900
See you later, Jim.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.260
Tell me, old man, when will the fog lift?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:32.760
That is... if the wind picks up,
the fog will disappear.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.580
So, when will the wind pick up?

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:40.770
That is, when the fog disappears.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.780
Damn, what heat!
It's like an oven.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.170
It smells like alcohol here, First Mate Arrow.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.920
I don't smell anything.

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.010
I can't take it anymore.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:20.780
Come on, Benbow.
It'll be better on deck.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.560
It's too hot.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.870
I'm tired of the heat...

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.970
Tell me, kid, where are we going?

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.890
Spit it out.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.680
I asked you where we're going.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.390
To an island, a Southern island!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.990
Is the rumor that it's an island of treasure true?

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.440
Where is it?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.900
I-I don't know.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.260
We may just be sailors,

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:16.460
but we want to know where to find it.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.500
Yeah!

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.370
It's because of the stubborn captain!

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:23.290
That scoundrel told him to shut up!

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:26.170
Him and those big shots.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:38.580
You gonna answer, kid?
And don't go telling the captain.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.390
Are you stupid?!
Leave me alone!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.700
"Leave him alone", is what Flint said.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.530
What is it, boatswain Anderson?
What's all the fuss?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.500
That you, Barbecue?

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.490
Nothing, nothing at all.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.540
Good.
Keep quiet then.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.660
We're sweating enough as it is.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.140
R-Right...

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.420
Hey guys, let's go.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.900
Y-Yeah, let's go.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.620
Thanks, Silver!

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:14.210
I told you, Jim, don't hang around on deck.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.500
On days without wind, everyone is on edge.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.500
But, Silver...

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.510
In this heat, you don't want to stay still?

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.620
Yeah...

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:24.170
Very well.
Then I'll take you with me.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.350
Where?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.500
Hey Barbecue, catch a big'un!

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.850
If you catch a whale,
we won't be able to eat it all!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:38.910
Got it.
Prepare your napkins and wait for us!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.830
I understand now.
So that's it.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.420
It's a privilege of being the master cook.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.360
As long as it doesn't interfere with the trip,

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:53.800
I have complete freedom to resupply.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.120
Jim, have you fished before?

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.260
No, this is my first time.
This'll be fun.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:03.100
Oh my, we can't see the Hispaniola anymore.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:07.340
Say, Silver, are you sure we can get back to the ship?

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:09.930
Well, time will tell...

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.110
Are you kidding?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:13.820
Of course I'm kidding.
Don't worry.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.980
Flint will guide us when we return.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.980
He's much more reliable than my old compass.

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:22.010
I see!
That puts me at ease.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.450
It's very quiet, I have goose bumps.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.670
The fish must be sleeping, eh Silver?

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.050
Look.
Flint is returning.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.050
Over there! Over there!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:45.560
Swordfish! Swordfish!
Lots of Swordfish!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.020
Over there! Over there!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.100
What?
A school of swordfish?

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:53.740
Jim, look straight ahead.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:55.610
You should be able to see them.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:18.400
It's definitely a school of swordfish!

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:20.760
Jim, hang on tight!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.650
Hold on!
Otherwise, we'll be swept away!

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.070
I hear you!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.500
Jim, I...

00:19:55.960 --> 00:20:01.040
In my young days I did some arm wrestling with the big Havana Black.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:03.280
An at least two meters tall giant!

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.430
The so-called Hercules of the docks.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.100
The stakes were high.
Spectators bet a lot of money.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.620
Who do you think won?

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:15.770
You, Silver!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.640
The match began that night...

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:22.620
...and at dawn it still hadn't stopped.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:27.440
The blood ran underneath our fingernails.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.220
As the betting folk had feared,

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.300
they called the match a draw.

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:33.600
You accepted?

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.710
Don't say such nonsense!
A man's battle never ends in a draw!

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:50.520
The bastard, he wants more!
He's coming!

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:54.850
Jim, another harpoon!

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.430
<i>We did it!</i>

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.700
We did it, Silver!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.600
Hurray! Hurray!
We did it!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.350
I know, I know.

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.770
We did it! We did it!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.630
Ahoy! We caught a lot!
Come see everyone!

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:06.560
Ahoy!

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:07.920
AHOY!

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.050
A—HOY!

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.060
Ahoy!

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:15.270
This isn't right, no one is coming.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.650
It's strange...

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:22.020
No one is on guard and
what's more, it's too quiet...

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:32.960
To      be        continued

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:39.030
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:39.030
Hey sea breeze

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:44.840
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:44.840
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:51.050
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:51.050
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:56.490
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:56.490
A word to my dear mother

00:22:56.490 --> 00:23:01.900
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:56.490 --> 00:23:01.900
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:07.360
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:07.360
And that my bag filled

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:12.990
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:12.990
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:18.850
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:18.850
Will be brought back

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:25.440
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:25.440
The sunset on my back

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:31.330
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:31.330
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:41.050
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:41.050
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:49.030
A ghost ship suddenly appeared before us!

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:54.410
On board, we find the man who disappeared at sea the day before, First Mate Arrow!

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:58.630
When a sailor is murdered on ship,
he always comes back for revenge.

00:23:59.170 --> 00:24:01.090
I have a hard time believing it,

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:04.460
but the ghost of the first mate seems to call out Silver.

00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:08.450
Next time on Treasure Island:
"The Ghost Ship Is Calling Me!"

00:24:08.450 --> 00:24:10.530
I know it's scary, but don't miss it!

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:14.120
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:14.120
*

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:14.120
Next time

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:14.120
Coming soon!

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:14.120
The Ghost Ship
Is Calling Me!
